model {
    extend cp.case-ingestion-subdomain {
        cpci = product {
            title 'Common Platform Civil Interface (CPCI)'
            description 'The civil-case ingestion path for Common Platform — used for cases flagged `isCivil=true` that carry non-criminal offence codes rather than criminal offences. Currently accepts civil charge and summons prosecutions from non-police civil prosecuting authorities (local authorities, regulatory bodies, and similar) via APIM, keyed by CJS Organisation Unit code. Complementary to CPPI (which handles criminal Non-Police Prosecutor cases), not a replacement for it. A future Enforcement Integration project (CCT-1222) plans to add a dedicated enforcement submission flow for Libra-Gob — this is currently in design/planning and not yet implemented.'

            staging-prosecutors-civil = microservice {
                title 'Staging Prosecutors Civil'
                technology 'Java EE'
                summary 'Ingests civil charge and summons prosecution submissions from non-police civil prosecuting authorities via APIM, stages them event-sourced, forwards them into the Prosecution Case File service as civil cases, and exposes a submission status query API'
                description """
A Java EE event-sourced CQRS service that provides Common Platform's civil-case ingestion channel. Accepts JSON submissions via Azure API Management authenticated per-prosecutor by CJS Organisation Unit code, and routes each submission into the Prosecution Case File service as either a single civil prosecution or a bulk (group) civil prosecution.

Civil cases on Common Platform are distinguished by the `isCivil=true` flag and carry non-criminal offence codes rather than criminal offence codes. They are prosecuted through the same magistrates' court process.

**Ingestion channels:**
- Accepts civil charge and summons prosecution submissions via APIM, keyed by a 7-character `prosecutingAuthority` CJS Organisation Unit code; APIM resolves the per-prosecutor system-user context from the inbound OU code before the request reaches the service
- Exposes a status query so submitters can poll for the outcome of each submission

**Single civil cases:**
- Behave like any other case on Common Platform, differing in that they carry non-criminal offence codes

**Bulk (group) civil cases:**
- API submission only
- A group of cases (a single defendant each) grouped under one "master defendant" (the rest are group members), sharing a single set of hearing details

**Internal pipeline:**
- **Event-sourced staging** — persists each submission as an event-sourced aggregate; an event processor converts accepted submissions into single civil or bulk (group) case-creation commands sent to the Prosecution Case File service, with the civil channel and `isCivil` flag set
- **Case ID resolution** — resolves the civil prosecutor case reference to a Common Platform case identifier via the System ID Mapper
- **Outcome subscription** — subscribes to Prosecution Case File events to track each submission's status (accepted, rejected, or accepted with warnings)
- **Viewstore** — maintains a thin submission-status view, surfaced via the status query API
- **Public event publication** — raises a public event when a charge prosecution is accepted, for downstream services to consume

Note: the planned Enforcement Integration (CCT-1222) will add a dedicated civil enforcement submission flow — carrying hearing details for auto-listing and an inbound submission path from Libra-Gob. This is currently in design/planning and is not part of the live implementation.
"""
                metadata {
                    language 'Java'
                    software-framework 'Java EE 8'
                }
                link https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-context-staging-prosecutors-civil 'Repository'

                this -> staging-prosecutors-civil-database
                this -> cp.case-management-system.prosecution-case-file-service 'sends civil single and group case-creation commands to, and subscribes to submission outcome events from'
                this -> cp.id-mapper-system.system-id-mapper 'resolves civil prosecutor URNs to Common Platform case identifiers using'
                this -[audit]-> cp.audit-system.audit-message-broker 'sends data to'
                this -[auth]-> cp.users-and-groups 'makes authorisation decisions using'

                non-police-prosecutors -> this 'submits civil charge and summons prosecutions to'
            }

            staging-prosecutors-civil-database = datastore {
                title 'Staging Prosecutors Civil Database'
                technology 'PostgreSQL'
                summary 'Stores civil prosecution submission aggregates and the thin submission status viewstore'
                style {
                    icon tech:postgresql
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
